WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.240
Your heart is shouting,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.260
"Be strong and sad!"

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.290
Just a little more,

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.180
Just a little bit more,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.720
Raise your hands!

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:27.550
I'm sure you won't realize it,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.760
But you're the same as you always were.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.490
You smiled at me,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:42.520
Like a leaf swaying in the wind.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:49.240
It seems as though my heart is going to explode.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.330
Your heart is shouting,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.020
"Be strong and sad!"

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.160
Just a little more,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.050
Just a little bit more,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.970
Raise your hands!

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:09.620
Someday, you will be gentle,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.820
And understand what I'm saying to you!

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.640
It'll be all right, no matter where you go,

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:21.660
This excitement will never stop!

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.910
Is that for real?

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.030
He looks so cute, and he's a playboy.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.330
Dammit. That bastard.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.830
How dare he do that to my idol!

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:11.980
It feels like I haven't had any time to collect my thoughts since I transferred here.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.240
Hey! Over here!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.580
Geez. You've made me wait so long!

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.120
C'mon! Let's go home together.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.340
What happened to my peaceful school life?

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:45.470
But then Kurotokage-sensei said that we weren't putting our hearts into our singing, and he got mad.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.390
And then he asked everyone to join the Drama Club.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.360
I don't understand why.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.230
Yeah.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:59.610
Not to brag, but I like karaoke, and I've gone with my friend Mayumi from the club.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.160
I always get a good score.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.490
And Kurotokage-sensei gets mad when he's teaching drama.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.500
I've got friends in the Drama Club.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.710
It's like he's possessed by a ghost.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.830
That's not too good, is it?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.250
I-I guess not.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.340
But it's not just Kurotokage-sensei.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.680
Just who in the world is this girl?

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.810
And our Home Ec. teacher is kind and...

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:32.400
I know that she waited for me at the entrance to school and asked to walk home with me, but...

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.230
When I first met her this morning, she suddenly...

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.860
You're destined to be my man!

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.240
That's what happened.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.860
Is she taking it at her own pace?

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.120
She doesn't listen to others.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.040
Since I often get injured during practice, I'm a bother to other people.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.000
But the teacher never gets mad at me and always treats me nicely.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.710
What's wrong? You're spacing out?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.710
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.130
Really?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.550
Do I talk too much?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.930
I want to hear more about you.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.430
Even if you ask me to...

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.310
Hey, hey, do you play any sports?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.640
What kind of songs do you like?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.270
Where do you usually play?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.150
Oh, I got a message.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.310
This is my mobile phone.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.240
Oh no. I completely forgot about it.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.360
Did something happen?

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.880
Sorry. Let's hurry.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.590
Run! There's no time to lose!

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.380
Just hurry!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.130
But...

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.090
You don't have to hold my hand!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:15.960
GOAL!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.920
I-I'm exhausted.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.840
Geez, you're so undependable.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.340
You should play some sports.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.930
E-Even if you tell me that...

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.100
But I'm glad.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:35.100
I wanted to try going home with my boyfriend.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:36.640
That's right.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.100
It feels good.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.730
Boyfriend?!

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.650
Anyway, I've gotta get going soon.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.650
Well, I see you tomorrow.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.320
Um...

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:54.830
Oh no. I forgot to ask him something so important.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.660
U-Um...

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.870
What is it this time?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.670
We haven't introduced ourselves yet.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.590
Oh dear.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.550
C-Come to think of it...

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.800
Well then, let me start.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.550
I'm Kasuga Tsukasa. I'm in Year 2, Class B.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.140
I'm in the Volleyball Club. It's nice to meet you.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.190
I'm Aoba Riku. I'm in Year 2, Class A.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.350
Aoba Riku.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.520
Riku.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.730
Riku-kun, right?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:22.860
Okay.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:23.820
I've remembered it!

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.860
Well, I'll be going back to school now.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.280
Going back...

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.700
Aren't you going home?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.660
I've got club now.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.200
Well, I'm gonna catch a bus now.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.960
What's up with her?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.460
That's right. I've gotta get back too!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.340
I can't take a bus from the station to my house.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.930
As I expected, it's a long way from the station to school.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.390
You're late, Tsukasa-san.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.640
I thought you were gonna skip training.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.440
I think I'd have missed training if it wasn't for your e-mail.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:04.480
Thanks.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.150
You really helped me out.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.440
You're welcome.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.870
But anyway, what happened?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.830
It's not like you to forget about volleyball practice.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.290
You wanna know?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.000
You got a boyfriend?!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.340
Geez. Don't shout like that.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.380
You're embarrassing me.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:35.180
But you just bumped into him when you met him, right?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.260
Yeah.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.640
How can you call him your boyfriend when that's all you did?

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.310
But my heart was pounding!

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.150
We were destined to meet like that!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:44.860
I don't know what you're going on about.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.520
Hey, hey, Ayame.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.860
What should I do as his girlfriend?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.820
We went home together...

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.530
I've never had a boyfriend before, so I'm not really sure what to do.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.250
W-Well, couples generally hang out together,

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.750
talk together during breaks, and call or e-mail each other when they can't see each other.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.000
I guess you could make lunch for him too...

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.050
I see.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.590
Yeah. Yeah!

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:11.840
I get it now.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.260
Okay! I'm gonna work hard starting tomorrow!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.930
Before you do that, you should work hard TODAY, too!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:20.890
Captain!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.730
Before you have fun with your boyfriends, do your penance for coming late.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.110
Run around the gym ten times.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.480
Y-Yes!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.490
Will Tsukasa really be all right?

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.340
Hey! Riku-kun!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.170
Morning, Riku-kun.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.430
Hey, I know this is sudden, but tell me your e-mail address.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:58.470
My e-mail address?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.470
Well, I don't mind...

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:04.600
And I'll tell you mine, so send me an e-mail right away, okay?

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.640
Let's see...

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:12.030
The morning I was teaching you two class in first class' classroom.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.610
Two of them, very close friends...

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.950
...to get the pieces of paper and pencils.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.370
What the?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.740
A message from Kasaya-san?!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:22.870
Aoba-kun.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.960
Turn off your mobile phone during class.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.460
S-Sorry!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.250
H-Hey, wait!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.590
Why am I getting so many messages?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.880
Hey! Get a hold of yourself!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.510
Even if you tell me to...

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.640
There're even more here.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:45.910
Moron---cant find if it is the evelope names it isnt worth the .2seconds that it last

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.650
Oh, Riku-kun.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.150
What're those letters?

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.230
Are they love letters?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.070
Oh, these are...

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.240
Oh, I'm so happy that my boyfriend's so popular.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.530
It's about that.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.620
Never mind that.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.530
You wanna go on a date this Sunday?

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.330
We've finally become lovers, too.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.500
Well, you just decided that on your own...

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.540
Let's see, should we go to an amusement park?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.920
Or see a movie?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.960
There's a good romance movie showing now.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.010
They've sent a lot of letters.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.760
Oh, Riku-kun.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.010
Are you going home now?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:24.850
Y-Yes.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.100
I've got club now, so e-mail me tonight!

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.530
So Aoba is Tsukasa's boyfriend.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.780
Tokimeki Memorial - Only Love!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.160
I'm Kasuga Tsukasa!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.790
Tokimeki Memorial - Only Love!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.460
I'm Ootomo Hiromi. Let's be friends!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.340
I brought lunch today.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.050
Did you make this for me?

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.390
Yes. I heard that you only eat bread every day.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:05.600
I thought you might be tired of that, so I made this with all my heart.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:07.600
Thank you.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.600
Please help yourself.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.020
Thanks for the food.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.530
Um... What is this green lump?!

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:23.160
That's a meatball simmered in propolis.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:23.160
(Note: Propolis is "bee glue", used by bees to make their hives.)

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.950
Doesn't it look healthy?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:25.820
What?

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:29.410
The rice has red peppers and capsicum in it to help you burn fat.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:34.880
The green omelet has green tea in it.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.210
C'mon! Eat up! Eat up!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:42.760
No... Even if it looks like this, it might taste good!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:44.390
Thanks for the food!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.520
Oh..  A mess? Let me clean up for you, Riku

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.000
I'm dying...!

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:04.320
Riku-kun!

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.370
What's wrong?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:07.950
It's nothing!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.120
By any chance, did it taste bad?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.210
Th-That's not true!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.040
It's great!

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.290
It's wonderful!

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.170
What a relief!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.300
I was quite worried, to be honest.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.720
It's the first time I've ever made lunch.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.510
This isn't good.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.760
I'm starting to lose consciousness...

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.470
Hey, Aoba!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.810
So that's where you were.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:33.980
S-Sorry!

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.520
My friends are calling me.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.690
I'll make lunch for you again.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.090
C-Cutting diarrhea..

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.600
surely...

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.410
Tokimeki Memo.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.660
Kasuga-san in Class B is a terrible cook.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.500
Should you really be leaving her alone?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.500
Kasuga-san and I aren't in a relationship like that.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.630
You're blushing, Aoba.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.750
L-Like I said, she just decided that on her own!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:06.430
Well, I managed to get some more information on Kasuga-san, so you've been a great help!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:11.810
But she can't cook, so it'll be harder for her to be your girlfriend.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:17.520
It would be rare for someone to cook as well as Amamiya-san!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.770
Oh, Amamiya-san can cook, too?

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.610
There's a story behind that.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.700
It happened during the culture festival last year.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.700
Our class made a stall for chocolate bananas,

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:39.250
and Amamiya-san used her best technique to create a unique "Golden Chocolate Banana"!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:45.800
It was so delicious that rumors began to spread, and the queue ran for miles!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:51.050
Even pastry chefs came to taste it!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.730
Amamiya-san is...

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:55.600
Oh my.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:56.850
What are you talking about?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.480
Amamiya-san!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.400
Oh, we were talking about Aoba's girlfriend.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.650
Like I said, that's a misunderstanding!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.990
You don't have to hide it from me.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.990
That rumor has already spread all over the school.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.910
But you should be careful about receiving messages during class.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:22.590
You shouldn't be obsessed about your girlfriend all the time, and you should work on your studies as well.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:26.170
Like I said, my girlfriend decided this on her own...

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.470
And I look forward to working with you at the sports fest next week.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.600
We're both running in the relay, after all.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.100
Y-Yes.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.100
I'm disappointed in you, Aoba.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.190
Shut up.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.900
I can't nap during the afternoon.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:55.910
Say, Tsukasa.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.960
I heard that you made lunch for Aoba-kun.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.960
Oh dear. You're in his class.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.250
Geez, I'm so embarrassed!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:06.840
Did you taste it?

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.260
No, I didn't, why?

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.890
There's some left, right?

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.010
Let me see.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.430
I knew it.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.850
If you feed this to him, he's gonna die!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.810
But he said it was good.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.690
Then try some.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:26.860
Okay.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.660
What the hell is this?!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.700
It tastes like paint!

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.240
I've never tasted paint before, but I'm sure it'd taste like this!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.040
Aoba-kun must have been forcing himself.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.960
And so were you. You're always saying that you're his girlfriend.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.960
You should think about how he feels, too.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:50.130
A girlfriend should think about how her boyfriend feels.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.720
Here we go!

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.430
Take that!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.640
That's not true!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:03.690
It's great!

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:04.860
It's wonderful!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.570
If it wasn't good, then he should have said so.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.120
Captain!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.290
What is it, Tsukasa?

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.870
I, Kasuga Tsukasa, will be skipping training today!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.500
Goodbye!

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.710
Hey! Tsukasa!

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:26.540
Wait!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:30.880
Harinui-sensei!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.220
Oh, Kasuga-san.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.050
This is unusual.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.510
Sensei, please teach me how to make a decent lunch!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.140
By any chance, do you want to make lunch for a boy?

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.560
Well... yes.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.440
I see. I'm happy for you.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:49.770
You'll be okay if you can cook these dishes.--cant find this one either

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.510
You'll be all right.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.350
Don't worry so much.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:22.430
Oh, yes!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.020
Well then.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.360
There were no grudge letters today.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.280
No messages either.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.820
What's Kasuga-san doing?

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.120
Hey, you over there.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.120
Who are you?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.040
Oh, sorry about that.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.870
I just saw that you were worrying.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.540
I haven't seen you here before.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:50.630
Are you a transfer student?

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.460
Yes, I'm Aoba Riku from Year 2, Class A.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.760
I'm the school nurse, Hoshino Naomi.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:56.930
It's nice to meet you.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.260
I see.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.220
Want to have some tea with me?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:11.940
Oh, I see.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.570
I never expected that your girlfriend would give you the cold shoulder so soon.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.320
She's not really my girlfriend...

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.160
But even so, why are you asking me this so suddenly?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.290
You have a crush on her, don't you?

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.620
I don't...

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.210
Don't worry about it.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.590
She'll come back to you as though nothing happened.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:34.750
Excuse me.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.420
Riku-kun!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:39.970
K-Kasuga-san?

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:49.100
Um... Well... Will you try my lunch again?

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.480
Y-Yes.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.120
H-How is it?

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.080
Is it good?

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.170
Yes, it's great!

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:16.420
All right!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:17.630
I did it!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.430
Harinui-sensei gave me special training, so I'm not gonna lose!

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.310
Oh, what a relief!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.220
I don't think it has anything to do with winning or losing.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:30.730
To me, it does.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:35.900
I'll keep making more lunches for you, so make sure you eat them, okay, Riku-kun?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.400
O-Okay.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.110
There.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.200
What should I make next?

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.200
French cuisine? Or Chinese?

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:46.330
Oh, but I should also try to make a traditional Japanese meal.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.290
I need to do some more special training with Harinui-sensei!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.920
Well, I guess things are okay like this.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.460
That's youth for you.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.510
Well, goodbye for now.

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.010
I'll see you tomorrow, Riku-kun.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.680
Yeah. Goodbye, Kasuga-san.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:12.940
Rain?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.150
Oh dear.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:24.910
I didn't bring an umbrella.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.750
Huh? I met her in the library, didn't I?

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.290
It's raining pretty hard.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:38.590
Is something wrong?

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.220
No, it's nothing.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.050
Are you taking shelter from the rain?

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:45.930
Do you ride your bike to school?

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:47.220
Yes.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:51.180
It takes about half an hour to walk home from here.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.140
I see. I don't think we should go now.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.440
It looks like the rain's gonna get worse.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.520
I like the rain.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.530
I like rainy days too.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.490
Because the scenery is different from usual.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.530
The colors and the scents are different, too.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.950
Oh, so that's what you meant.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.370
This scenery is different from what I usually see.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:19.960
The green colors look fresher, and the scents are stronger than usual.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.680
Is something wrong?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.640
Oh, it's nothing.

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.060
O-Oh no!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.560
Are you all right?

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.190
Oh, this is nothing.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:41.070
Please use this, Aoba-san.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.900
Th-Thank you.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.160
Huh? How did you know my name?

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:48.620
Well...

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:50.070
I think the rain's gonna stop.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.700
I'll be going now.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:54.580
Oh, your handkerchief!

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.080
What's your name?

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:58.330
Um...

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.340
I'm Yayoi Mina in Year 1, Class C.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.130
I'm in the Swimming Club.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.960
Well then, goodbye.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.850
Yayoi Mina-san, eh?

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:37.210
When the morning sunlight streams through the window,

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:42.250
I immediately think of you.

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:54.220
Our love began at first sight.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:23:00.230
We have a bright future!

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:06.650
Because you are my destined man!

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:17.330
I've always been searching for the feeling which broke my smile.

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.340
I have grasped a piece of the miracle which fell into this world

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:30.260
I will run toward you, my love!

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:35.930
When we are together, we can overcome any obstacle!

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:42.560
Our love is still young, but it's my treasure!

00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:54.030
Sensei, I've lost confidence in myself.

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:55.450
You'll be all right.

00:23:55.870 --> 00:23:58.450
You have a very powerful weapon.

00:23:59.200 --> 00:23:59.790
Weapon?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.790
You look really stylish in your swimsuit!

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:04.670
Come on! Give it a try!

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:05.840
Say "Onii-chan".

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:07.880
O-Onii-chan?

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:09.340
Now use "tan"!

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:10.050
(Note: "tan" is an expression of endearment that implies greater closeness than "chan".)

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:09.670
"tan" is an expression of endearment that implies more closeness than "chan".)

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:13.590
